@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Durable outbound retry, permanent failure und no-duplicate event

autonumber
actor "Workspace client" as Client
participant "Current Workspace API" as API
database "Canonical state + outbox + outbound operation" as DB
participant "Realtime Connector\nwhole-account lease" as Bridge
participant "Private Workspace API\ncurrent realm mTLS" as PrivateAPI
participant "Zulip" as Zulip
database "Durable ready events" as Events
participant "WebSocket dispatcher" as WS

Client -> API : current provider-backed mutation
API -> DB : canonical mutation + outbox + durable outbound op
API --> Client : 2xx/201 = local commit, not provider confirmation

loop Until confirmed or permanent
  Bridge -> PrivateAPI : mTLS claim due op(account generation)
  PrivateAPI -> DB : verify certificate identity + account lease;\nlease due operation
  PrivateAPI --> Bridge : operation + lease generation
  Bridge -> Zulip : provider call(operation UUID, causation, expected revision)
  alt transient / ambiguous
    Zulip --> Bridge : timeout / 429 / temporary failure
    Bridge -> PrivateAPI : mTLS retryable receipt
    PrivateAPI -> DB : conditional attempts/backoff update
  else provider rejection
    Zulip --> Bridge : permanent error
    Bridge -> PrivateAPI : mTLS permanent receipt(code, safe reason)
    PrivateAPI -> DB : conditional permanent_failed
  else confirmed response/echo
    Zulip --> Bridge : confirmed state/revision
    Bridge -> PrivateAPI : mTLS confirmed receipt
    PrivateAPI -> DB : conditional confirmed state
  end
end

alt Actual client-visible transition
  DB -> Events : state/projection + one ready event in one transaction
  WS -> Events : replay/live read
  WS -> Client : at-least-once current-contract event
else duplicate / stale / echo-only
  DB -> DB : no new outbox or ready event
end

note over Bridge,Zulip
  Last confirmed wins; delete wins stale edit.
  Retry survives process/lease failover with same operation UUID.
  Echo confirms causation and never loops back.
end note

note over Bridge,PrivateAPI
  Current mTLS certificate authenticates Bridge identity.
  Whole-account lease/fencing separately authorizes each claim/receipt.
end note

note over DB,WS
  delivery_class/notification metadata preserved.
  Dispatcher delivers; Bridge never owns public WebSocket connections.
end note

@enduml
